        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): avoid synthetic overflow in tool-heavy sessions",
        "body": "Closes #107655\n\nRelated: #107821\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where long-lived, tool-heavy sessions could discard a provider-acceptable projected prompt and trigger whole-session compaction when conservative local character estimates reported pressure.\n\nOn current `main`, a restored session with twelve 50k-character tool results manufactured a local context overflow before provider submission. Recovery compacted and persistently rewrote the session even though the controlled provider accepted the projected prompt.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nGeneric aggregate, preflight, and tool-loop character pressure now remains prompt-shaping and diagnostic input rather than proof of context overflow. Explicit opt-in mid-turn recovery remains unchanged. When a provider actually rejects context, the existing recovery path records the final provider request identity and prevents resending a byte-identical rejected payload while allowing materially changed retries.\n\nThis addresses the common false-positive authority across all three generic gates. #107821 is a useful narrow mitigation for successful aggregate replacement, but it leaves the normal preflight estimator and always-on tool-loop character guard able to manufacture the same overflow without a provider rejection.\n\nNo configuration, protocol, provider identity, public API, or persisted-session format changes.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I traced the runtime and upstream Codex contracts, reviewed every accepted autoreview finding, and understand the implementation and proof.\n\n## User Impact\n\nTool-heavy sessions can submit their bounded provider prompt without premature compaction or history loss. Genuine provider context rejections still use bounded recovery, and an identical rejected request cannot enter a retry loop.\n\n## Evidence\n\nDeterministic Gateway reproduction on the current-main baseline:\n\n- Accumulated twelve real 50k-character `exec` results under a 1.05M model window.\n- Restarted the Gateway with the same model set to 272k, then sent a normal follow-up.\n- Baseline made 15 provider calls, triggered synthetic compaction, and retained only 1/12 historical tool results.\n\nExact final patch on Blacksmith Testbox via Crabbox:\n\n- The same real Gateway restart scenario passed in 14 provider calls.\n- All 12/12 historical tool results and the newest sentinel reached the follow-up request.\n- The follow-up completed without rerunning tools.\n- Private reproduction harness remained under ignored `.artifacts/` and is intentionally not part of this PR.\n\nRegression and repository proof:\n\n- Focused prompt projection, admission, overflow, and compaction suite: 394/394 passed across 14 files.\n- Fresh Codex autoreview: no accepted/actionable findings.\n- `pnpm check:changed` on Testbox: passed, including production/test typechecks and full selected lint/policy gates (13m50s).\n- `pnpm build` on Testbox: passed (1m22s).\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Testbox run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29617210821\n",
        "branch": "fix/provider-authoritative-context-pressure",
